    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's a good question. Really, a lot of that is in our own hands. What are we going to be willing to do? If you look throughout scripture, that's a great place to go for answers and direction. Israel was given chance after chance after chance by a long suffering and patient, holy God, saying, come back to me, my people. Come back, come back, come back. and the warnings that came from prophets. If you don't return to God and reject the idolatry and the false gods that you have taken, you will be spewed out of the land. We are not Israel. America is an Israel and Christians aren't Israel. So I'm not saying that, but I think that it's a pattern and a directive. When we see that we have been so obviously blessed by a holy God, when many people, a critical mass at least, returning toward him, I think it's also prudent to say that it just may be that the Lord may relent and give us a reprieve. But we don't know. No matter what, our call is to be faithful. That is our call. Be obedient, be faithful, no matter what. The other thing I want to say, Todd, is I want to encourage your audience. Don't despair. Don't despair and don't give up. I read the same paper that you read. I see the same horrifying stories and statistics that you see. That's all the more reason for us to keep our mind on the things of God. If people haven't downloaded the Bible app, I highly encourage you to do it. Just this morning, I spent an hour walking around Virginia Beach, walking around the campus of Virginia Beach of Regent University. I had my earphones on. I was listening to the Book of Proverbs all morning. I thought, Lord, I need wisdom. I need wisdom. What better place to go than the Book of Proverbs? I",
